<title>UK: UK ave weekly wages up 4.2 pct in yr to April.</title>
<headline>UK ave weekly wages up 4.2 pct in yr to April.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK average gross weekly earnings of full-time adults rose by 4.2 percent on the year to April 1996, the Office for National Statistics said on Thursday.</p>
<p>That increase represented an average weekly wage of 352 stg. Part-time weekly earnings rose less quickly, by 1.5 percent to stand at 107 stg, for an average of 19 hours worked per week.</p>
<p>Full-time women's earnings increased by half a percentage point more than men's while earnings of full-time non-manual workers increased by almost a full percentage point more than those of manual workers, the ONS said.  </p>
<p>The average weekly wage for full-time women workers was 283 stg, compared with 392 stg for men.</p>
